/-! # Universal weak schematic density of the jets of a smooth section

Source: Conrad, Reductive group schemes, Definition 2.1.7, printed p.61,
and proof of Proposition 2.1.6, printed pp.62--63
(blueprint: lem-sfb-smooth-section-universal-jet-density).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The infinitesimal neighborhoods of a section of a smooth affine morphism with
nonempty geometrically connected fibers are weakly schematically dense after every
base change. The two projection equations express factorization of the canonical
base-changed quotient immersion. An isomorphism of that closed immersion means equality
with the whole ambient closed subscheme, including its scheme structure.

Source: Conrad, Reductive group schemes, Definition 2.1.7, printed p.61,
and proof of Proposition 2.1.6, printed pp.62--63
(blueprint: lem-sfb-smooth-section-universal-jet-density).

Proof:
1. The algebraic-closure criterion
   (lem-weil-geometrically-connected-algebraic-closure) gives geometric connectedness.
   The open component through the section supplied by
   lem-sbc-smooth-section-component-geometrically-irreducible is the whole scheme,
   because every fiber is connected. Thus all fibers are geometrically irreducible.
2. For any A-algebra C, the affine pullback formula
   (lem-weil-pbc-fibre-product-affine-spectra) identifies the base change with
   Spec(B tensor_A C). By lem-sfb-smooth-section-finite-jets, its jet quotients are
   (B/J^(n+1)) tensor_A C. The original jet quotients are finite locally free,
   hence flat by def-pc-finite-locally-free and lem-weil-pbc-flat-ring-map-iff-flat-affine.
   Smoothness survives base change by lem-pc-smooth-flat,
   lem-sfb-scheme-flat-smooth-point-base-change and lem-weil-pbc-smooth-local-on-source;
   geometric irreducibility of the fibers survives by definition.
3. If C is Noetherian, B tensor_A C is Noetherian: use
   lem-weil-pbc-lfp-affine-opens-finite-presentation, pure tensor generation, and
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra-noetherian. Put N = intersection_n J_C^(n+1).
   By lem-weil-pbc-krull-intersection-localization, N vanishes on an open
   neighborhood V of the section.
4. V meets every irreducible fiber in a nonempty dense open. Apply
   lem-sfb-smooth-fibrewise-dense-open-base-change with identity base change:
   the structure sheaf embeds into its restriction pushed forward from V.
   Every element of N vanishes on V, so N = 0, also for nonreduced C.
5. For arbitrary C, express an element b of N as a finite sum of pure tensors,
   and let C0 be the subalgebra generated by their finitely many coefficients.
   It is Noetherian by lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra-noetherian. A lift b0 over
   C0 vanishes in every jet quotient: the inclusions of their tensors from C0
   into C are injective by flatness and lem-weil-pbc-flat-tensor-exact.
   Hence b0 belongs to every J_C0^(n+1). Step 4 gives b0 = 0 and therefore b = 0.
   The same C0 works for every n; no infinite intersection is tensor-commuted.
6. Cover T by affine opens. The closed immersion is locally defined by an ideal K
   (def-weil-closed-immersion). The two projection equations say K is contained
   in every J_C^(n+1). Step 5 gives K = 0. The ideal sheaf vanishes on the cover,
   hence globally, so the closed immersion is an isomorphism. -/
theorem Smooth.isIso_of_section_jets_factor
    (A B : Type u) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    (p : Spec (.of B) ⟶ Spec (.of A)) [Smooth p] [LocallyOfFinitePresentation p]
    (ε : B →+* A) (hε : Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom ε) ≫ p = 𝟙 (Spec (.of A)))
    (hgeom : ∀ s : Spec (.of A),
      ConnectedSpace ↥(pullback p
        (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
          (algebraMap ((Spec (.of A)).residueField s)
            (AlgebraicClosure ((Spec (.of A)).residueField s)))) ≫
          (Spec (.of A)).fromSpecResidueField s)))
    {T : Scheme.{u}} (g : T ⟶ Spec (.of A))
    {Z : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ pullback p g) [IsClosedImmersion i]
    (hjets : ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ l :
      pullback
        (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker ε ^ (n + 1)))) ≫ p)
        g ⟶ Z,
      l ≫ i ≫ pullback.fst p g =
        pullback.fst
          (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker ε ^ (n + 1)))) ≫ p)
          g ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker ε ^ (n + 1)))) ∧
      l ≫ i ≫ pullback.snd p g =
        pullback.snd
          (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker ε ^ (n + 1)))) ≫ p)
          g) :
    IsIso i := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
